Z||000011||Cliff Pennock||11-17-2001||05:06 PM||||Well, I agree to a point. I don't mind reading through a posting filled with spelling- or grammatical errors. The only thing that bothers me <B>tremendously</B> is that these postings are often made by adult Americans, Canadians, British or other people whom's native language <B>is</B> English.<P>My spelling and grammar isn't perfect, but <B>my</B> excuse is that I'm Dutch. I don't read, hear or speak English all day long. I wasn't educated in the English language 5 days per week at school. I find it inexcusable that people can't spell in their own language. I can understand if you misspell difficult words, but if you <I>consistently</I> spell the most basic words wrong, well, then you're either dyslexic, or your education was a total waste of money.<P>l337 74lk was invented by kids to hide the fact that they spent way too much time behind their computer when they should be studying. They can't spell worth 5h1t.<BR>||||reg||1
