Z||000014||Mach10||11-17-2001||07:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B> Call me naive, but [b]what</B> was invented by kids...??<P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>'Leet speak... Psuedo-hacker talk. Basically making words out of characters from the poop-chute end of the ASCII library, and warping the words...<P>i 0\|/n J0o, B!$@tc||<P>And the like... It's an unfortunate spin-off from AOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||167.1.120.20||reg||1
Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||11-17-2001||07:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B> Call me naive, but [b]what</B> was invented by kids...??<BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"l337 741k" = "Leet talk" = "Elite talk"<P>Apparantly, you are the king if you can write words using anything <B>but</B> the original 26 characters from the alphabet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I don't know - maybe I'm just turning into a dinosaur but in my highschool days, it was cool if you could recite something from Shakespeare or if you knew Pi in more than 30 decimals (3.14159265358979323846264338327950288 - I still know that by heart, hope I still got it right though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||1
