Z||000018||rogergarrison||11-18-2001||06:30 AM||||first, in your example, those could all just be simple typos. I do those myself. Sometimes your mind moves faster than typing fingers. I use the (') to bring attention to the word or when its used to mean something similar. I dont (&lt; ) use it in words like this because it seems so unimportant. Everyone knows what I mean. And, I sometimes just ignore using caps to start a sentence. This is just a form of communication, so be more tolerant, I am. BTW, is there going to be a test later? Are you a college english professor?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||Monkeyman||11-18-2001||07:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B> "l337 741k" = "Leet talk" = "Elite talk"<P>Apparantly, you are the king if you can write words using anything [b]but</B> the original 26 characters from the alphabet.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I don't know - maybe I'm just turning into a dinosaur but in my highschool days, it was cool if you could recite something from Shakespeare or if you knew Pi in more than 30 decimals (3.14159265358979323846264338327950288 - I still know that by heart, hope I still got it right though   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm still confused as to the reason why anyone would even try to communicate using characters instead of letters.  Oooo...It's like secret code.  (Where <I>is</I> my Batman Decoder Ring???)<P>I can recite Pi up through about 6 decimals, but I never use it so I have no reason to remember it.  (If you don't use it, you lose it.)  I enjoyed quoting Shakespeare, but most of the kids in school around here were much more impressed if you knew how to neuter a cow or shoe a horse.  (Sorry, but...<B>boring</B>!)  What do you expect from a school that gives you credit for being in FFA (Future Farmers of America)?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
