Z||000069||Voytek||11-20-2001||03:14 PM||||Correct spelling, cohesion and punctuation indicate the education and intelect level of the postee.  If I am debating a point with someone who demonstrates a much lower level of intelect (in this case conveyed by their careless spelling, etc.) then I feel that I am wasting my keyboard by posting a reply.<P>Yes, I know.  All of you who claim that you simply don't CARE about spelling will jump on me for this.  Sorry, but I don't buy this attitude.  If you have a good point to make, make it legible.<P>Yes, there is the other side of the coin.  The 'big' words (we've seen a member use an abundance of those).  It is not a sign of intelligence - it's a sign of a pea-brain trying to look bigger and superior.<P>BTW, English is my 3rd language and I don't use the spellcheck.  Don't tell me that English is too difficult to learn.<P>All people new to the language will have some difficulties but, so far, no one on PFF has blaimed their bad spelling / grammar on being new - just plain laziness.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
